      "title": "15. Final recap",
      "content": [
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Remember the main difference between these five steps:"
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Partition — divide the disk."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Format — create the file system."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Mount — make the file system accessible through a directory."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Persist — configure automatic mounting in /etc/fstab."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "Swap — prepare and activate disk space for memory management."
        },
        {
          "level": 0,
          "text": "For your RHCSA preparation, practise the complete workflow on an additional virtual disk in your RHEL lab. Never experiment with partitioning or formatting on your real system disk."
